        "sourceText": "# The Grand Tournament\n\nTime limit: $4$ seconds. Memory limit: $1024$ MB. Standard input and standard output.\n\nThe First Grand Tournament of Automated Driving has begun!\n\nThe experimental field is an axis-aligned rectangle in the plane, with bottom-left corner $(x_l,y_l)$ and top-right corner $(x_r,y_r)$. Two line segments $A$ and $B$ lie strictly inside the rectangle. They may have points in common. A car inside the rectangle is treated as a point.\n\nIn this subtask, the car must remain at equal distances from the two segments throughout its movement. The distance from a point $P$ to a segment $Q$ is the minimum Euclidean distance from $P$ to any point of $Q$.\n\n![diagram](grand-tournament-diagram.png)\n\nThe figure illustrates the sample data. Find the area of all valid positions of the car inside the rectangle.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains the number of test cases $T$ ($1\\leq T\\leq10^5$).\n\nFor each test case, the first line contains four integers $x_l,y_l,x_r,y_r$ ($-1000\\leq x_l<x_r\\leq1000$, $-1000\\leq y_l<y_r\\leq1000$), specifying the rectangle.\n\nEach of the next two lines contains four integers $x_1,y_1,x_2,y_2$, specifying one segment with endpoints $(x_1,y_1)$ and $(x_2,y_2)$. They satisfy $x_1,x_2\\in(x_l,x_r)$ and $y_1,y_2\\in(y_l,y_r)$.\n\nThe two endpoints of each individual segment are distinct.\n\n## Output\n\nFor each test case, output one real number: the area of valid positions. The absolute or relative error must not exceed $10^{-9}$.\n\nFormally, if your answer is $a$ and the jury's answer is $b$, the answer is accepted if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{|a-b|}{\\max\\{1,|b|\\}}\\leq10^{-9}.\n$$\n",
